# Pulse Architecture

Pulse is a real-time observability platform for mobile apps, built on OpenTelemetry.

## Monorepo Layout

| Directory | Service | Tech | Port |
|-----------|---------|------|------|
| `backend/server/` | REST API | Java 17, Vert.x 4.5, Guice, Maven | 8080 |
| `backend/pulse-alerts-cron/` | Alert evaluation cron + daily batch jobs | Java/Vert.x | 4000 |
| `backend/ingestion/` | OTEL Collector configs + ClickHouse schema | YAML/SQL | — |
| `backend/session-capture-service/` | Session replay HTTP ingest (Rust) | Rust | 3400 |
| `backend/session-replay-ingestion/` | Kafka → S3 + ClickHouse consumer | Node.js | — |
| `backend/heatmap-screenshot-ingestion/` | Heatmap screenshots (Kafka → S3); optional external Redis quota/dedupe | Node.js | — |
| `pulse-ui/` | Dashboard | React 18, TypeScript, Mantine v7 | 3000 |
| `pulse_ai/` | AI agent (`deploy` service `pulse-ai-agent` by default; standalone compose for AI-only dev) | Python, Google ADK + Gemini | 8000 |
| `pulse-android-otel/` | Android SDK | Kotlin, OpenTelemetry | — |
| `pulse-ios-otel/` | iOS SDK (PulseKit) | Swift, OpenTelemetry | — |
| `pulse-react-native-otel/` | React Native SDK | TypeScript | — |
| `deploy/` | Docker Compose, scripts, Terraform | — | — |
| `deploy/observability-otel-prometheus-tempo/` | Optional OTEL → Prometheus + Tempo + Grafana (dev); not part of default stack | Compose | see folder `README.md` |

## Data Flow

```
Mobile SDKs → OTEL Collector (4317/4318) → ClickHouse (otel DB)
Optional: pulse-server / pulse-alerts-cron (env `PULSE_BACKEND_OTEL_ENABLED`) → OTLP on host (e.g. 14318) → optional `observability-otel-prometheus-tempo` stack → Tempo / Prometheus (do not bind 14317/14318 alongside Vector on the same host without changing ports)
Mobile SDKs → Session capture API (:3400) → Kafka → Session replay ingestion → MinIO (S3) + ClickHouse
Custom Events → Vector (14317/14318) → S3 (Parquet) → Athena / BigQuery  [Vector optional: service is commented out in `deploy/docker-compose.yml` by default; uncomment + VECTOR_ENABLED=true]
Session replay / heatmap → Kafka → pulse-heatmap-screenshot-ingestion → S3 bucket `heatmap-assets` (keys under `heatmap-screenshots/`); optional external Redis for quota / dedupe
```

## Databases

- **MySQL 8** (`pulse_db`): metadata — interactions, alerts, configs, symbol files, athena jobs, analytics_jobs
- **ClickHouse 24.8** (`otel`): analytics — `otel_traces`, `otel_logs`, OTLP metrics (`otel_metrics_gauge`, `otel_metrics_sum`, `otel_metrics_summary`, `otel_metrics_histogram`, `otel_metrics_exp_histogram`, unified read view `otel_metrics`), `stack_trace_events`, `project_monthly_usage` (+ MVs), `root_cause_cache` (RCA cache; column `ProjectId`), `interaction_heatmaps_daily` (heatmap table + MV defined in `clickhouse-otel-schema.sql`)

## Auth

**Production:** Google OAuth 2.0 → JWT (access 24h, refresh 30d). Tokens in cookies on frontend.

**Dev Mode** (when `GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED=false`):
- Bypasses Google OAuth
- Mock users: `mock-user-1`, `mock-user-2` (pre-seeded in MySQL + OpenFGA)
- Default project: `default-project` with hardcoded API key (`DEV_MODE_API_KEY`)
- Auto-initialized on startup via `DevModeInitService`

## Cross-Cutting Concerns

Alert metrics span: MySQL schema → backend `ServiceError`/service/DAO → alerts cron → UI form → AI metric registry. Changes usually need updates across multiple services.
